{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevFjy4MRJJj1izJBAiQL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Analysis Summary\n\n**Requirement, restated:** Add an idempotent `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint that moves CREATED shipments to CONFIRMED status, returns 409 for CANCELLED shipments, 404 for missing shipments, and succeeds without change when confirming already-CONFIRMED shipments.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment model: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-14`\n- ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED): `Shipment.kt:23-27`\n- ShipmentController (existing create, get, list endpoints): `ShipmentController.kt:20-56`\n- InMemoryShipmentRepository: `ShipmentRepository.kt:11-27`\n- ApiException classes (ResourceNotFoundException, ConflictException): `ApiExceptions.kt:18-24`\n- ErrorCode enum: `ApiError.kt:31-37`\n- GlobalExceptionHandler: `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:13-28`\n- Tests: `ShipmentControllerTest.kt:23-84`\n\n**Conventions:**\n- Controllers throw typed ApiExceptions which the GlobalExceptionHandler translates to ApiError responses\n- Error messages follow pattern: \"No {resource} with id '{id}'\" or \"A {resource} with id '{id}' {state}\"\n- Tests use MockMvc with `.andExpect(jsonPath(...))` assertions\n- Successful responses use `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(...)`\n- ErrorCode enum is the single source of error codes\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` – must add error code for \"cannot confirm cancelled shipment\" (409 case)\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` – must add the `/confirm` endpoint\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` – must add tests for all four cases\n\n**Risks:**\n- Idempotence: confirming already-CONFIRMED must not fail\n- Missing error code for the cancelled state 409 case\n- Status code consistency across failure modes\n\n**Open questions:** None – the requirement is clear on all cases.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED` to the ErrorCode enum. This codes the 409 Conflict case for attempting to confirm a CANCELLED shipment, maintaining the pattern where error codes describe the specific violation.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new method `confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String)` that:\n   - Takes only a path variable (no request body needed)\n   - Retrieves the shipment or throws ResourceNotFoundException if not found\n   - Returns 409 ConflictException if status is CANCELLED\n   - If status is CREATED, updates to CONFIRMED and saves\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, returns unchanged (idempotent)\n   - Returns ResponseEntity with the shipment and 200 OK status\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four new test methods covering:\n   - `confirm_moves_created_shipment_to_confirmed` – verifies status changes and is persisted\n   - `confirm_idempotent_on_already_confirmed_shipment` – confirms already-CONFIRMED returns same state unchanged\n   - `confirm_rejects_cancelled_shipment_with_409` – verifies ConflictException with correct error code\n   - `confirm_rejects_unknown_shipment_id_with_404` – verifies ResourceNotFoundException with correct error code\n\n**Alternatives considered and rejected:**\n\n- *Alternative 1: Add separate method for each state transition* – Would create methods like `confirmCreated`, `reConfirm`, `rejectCancelled`. Rejected because the requirement asks for a single `/confirm` endpoint that handles all cases, and this would violate the unified interface.\n\n- *Alternative 2: Use a separate service layer* – Could extract confirm logic to `ShipmentService`. Rejected because the existing codebase (create, get, list) has no service layer and the repository operations here are trivial; adding one would be unrelated refactoring outside the scope.\n\n- *Alternative 3: Make CANCELLED → CONFIRMED allowed with a validation exception* – Could accept the confirm but throw a validation error. Rejected because the requirement explicitly states \"Confirming a shipment that is CANCELLED is rejected with HTTP 409\", which is a Conflict (state violation), not a Validation error (input violation).\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Action | Status | Response |\n|------|-------|--------|--------|----------|\n| Unknown ID | `POST /shipments/S-missing/confirm` | Lookup fails | 404 | `ResourceNotFoundException` → ApiError with `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND` |\n| CANCELLED → confirm | `POST /shipments/S-cancelled/confirm` | Status check fails | 409 | `ConflictException` → ApiError with `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED` |\n| CREATED → confirm | `POST /shipments/S-created/confirm` | Status updated to CONFIRMED, saved | 200 | Full Shipment JSON with `status: \"CONFIRMED\"` |\n| CONFIRMED → confirm | `POST /shipments/S-confirmed/confirm` | No update needed | 200 | Same Shipment JSON with `status: \"CONFIRMED\"` (unchanged) |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **test_confirm_moves_created_shipment_to_confirmed**: Create shipment (status CREATED), POST `/confirm`, assert 200 OK and `status: \"CONFIRMED\"`, then GET to verify persistence\n2. **test_confirm_idempotent_on_already_confirmed**: Create and confirm shipment, POST `/confirm` again, assert 200 OK and status still CONFIRMED (unchanged)\n3. **test_confirm_rejects_cancelled_shipment_with_409**: Directly set a shipment to CANCELLED in repository, POST `/confirm`, assert 409 Conflict with error code `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED`\n4. **test_confirm_rejects_unknown_shipment_id_with_404**: POST `/confirm` on non-existent ID, assert 404 Not Found with error code `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND`\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes. Let me start with the error code:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1019,"cache_read_input_tokens":18